<article class="env-lemma" id="0DI4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DI4">Lemma <span data-tag="0DI4">36.35.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is flat and locally of finite presentation. A perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is $S$-perfect. If $K, M \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$, then $K \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X}^\mathbf {L} M$ is $S$-perfect if $K$ is perfect and $M$ is $S$-perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      First proof: reduce to the affine case using Lemma <a href="/tag/0DI2" data-tag="0DI2">36.35.3</a> and then apply More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DHU" data-tag="0DHU">15.85.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>